	<key>readme</key>
	<string># alfred-readwise
## An Alfred Workflow for your [Readwise](https://readwise.io/) account
![](alfred-readwise.png)
Complete readme [here](https://github.com/giovannicoppola/alfred-readwise/blob/main/README.md)

# What's new in 0.4 ✨
- **Readwise Reader support.** Search your saved articles alongside your highlights. Set `Search Platform` to Reader, or to Readwise and Readwise Reader for both. Reader documents are matched on title, author and site name.
- **Refreshes are near-instant.** The database now syncs only what changed instead of downloading everything, turning a refresh that took minutes into well under a second.
- **A refresh could previously never finish.** Hitting Readwise's rate limit retried forever, and every keystroke could start another sync that rate-limited the others. Fixed.
- **Searching a word with an apostrophe no longer fails**, and TLS certificate verification is enabled again.
- **Highlights created from Alfred are now searchable straight away** — they used to be saved without their text.
- **Pillow is now optional.** A missing `PIL` module no longer stops the workflow; you just lose the QuickLook previews.

# Motivation ✅
- Quickly list, search, and open your Readwise highlights and Reader documents
- Add new highlights to your account through Alfred

# Setting up ⚙️

### Needed
- Alfred 5 with Powerpack license
- A [Readwise](https://readwise.io) license
- Python3
- Download `alfred-readwise` [latest release](https://github.com/giovannicoppola/alfred-readwise/releases/latest)

## Settings
In Alfred, open the 'Configure Workflow' menu in `alfred-readwise` preferences:
- **Main Keyword** — launches the workflow (default: `!r`)
- **Force refresh keyword** (default: `readwise:refresh`) — syncs only what changed, normally instant
- **Full rebuild keyword** (default: `readwise:rebuild`) — downloads everything again. Slower, but the only way to drop highlights you deleted in Readwise. Also runs automatically every 30 days
- **Readwise token** — copy it [here](https://readwise.io/access_token)
- **What to show**: `books`, `tweets`, `supplementals`, `articles`, `podcasts`
- **Refresh rate** in days (default: `30`)
- **Title for new highlights** added via Alfred (default: `Highlights from Alfred`)
- **Search Platform**: Readwise highlights (default), Readwise Reader, or both
- **Search Scope**: `Main` searches highlight text only; `Include metadata` also searches book title and author. Applies to highlights only — Reader documents are always searched by title, author and site name
- **Open Reader documents in**: `Browser` (default) or `Reader app`. Only relevant when Reader documents are in your results; falls back to the browser if the app is not installed

# Basic Usage 📖
- launch with the keyword (default: `!r`), or a custom hotkey
- type `--reader` or `--readwise` anywhere in the query to restrict results to one platform

## On a highlight
- &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; copy and show in Large Type
- &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; open the source URL
- &lt;kbd&gt;^&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; open the highlight on Readwise
- &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;Y&lt;/kbd&gt; Quick Look the highlight

## On a Reader document
- &lt;kbd&gt;^&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; open the document in Reader (browser or app, per the setting above)
- &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; open the original article

Create new highlights via the Universal Action.</string>
